      {
        "id": 632608,
        "name": "Sayan Ghosh",
        "username": "sayan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discourse.onlinedegree.iitm.ac.in/sayan/{size}/112713_2.png",
        "created_at": "2025-05-28T05:05:25.285Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If you resolve <a href=\"http://youtube.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">youtube.com</a>, you get an IP that opens google, and not youtube, hence the answer should be NO. If it were to open youtube’s page, then the answer would be YES.</p>\n<p>Obviously it will not open google if youtube and google are not related. Google owning youtube is the reason it opens google. Since it does not open youtube, so the answer is no.</p>",
