  "all_posts": [
    {
      "id": 632605,
      "name": "Nandan",
      "username": "23f1000539",
      "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/2/bbce88/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2025-05-28T05:02:16.093Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This is specific to BPT problem no. 4. We have been asked to resolve the given domain names into IP addresses and check, whether the IPs are we able to open the corresponding website.<br>\nOne of the domain name given was <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">www.youtube.com</a> and the IP address obtained from resolving the domain name, did open <a href=\"http://google.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">google.com</a>. Considering that Youtube is a platform owned by google the output should be YES. But in the BPT problem if we put YES the evaluation fails.</p>\n<p>I was having this discussion with <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/chaitanya353535\">@chaitanya353535</a> sir in the TA session on tuesday 27th May 2025.<br>\n<a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/sayan\">@sayan</a> sir kindly look into this.<br>\nThank you.</p>",
